{"type":"message","id":"d894441e","parentId":"e254dac6","timestamp":"2026-04-03T18:52:39.690Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0777a1a86320e9530169d00c63c4ec819181e3abe5f2a53b60\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp0AxkyD6TbafR79sd8lNb4dQLR3hqOsoZzAcyXACRv4GOIJ8w2Hmwrn6Pxwrmp6CeavSJ-VNvG0fN79HuFq19078JVtnG5jjaljLibwRTgpUiftSwSG3QRhsBkFDIFuLhiE4qH7uvPwin3Ot7afwaLK2YqlPBEYS4adl-6KHsHLKk47UZdJkOLzM1hrCG-iF5cHgVjHYfYaPrpJKW645v0oqe6LVMuw2meNPBtI2ujPblbvWJUfQ3oHAuUhOAxweKdEhkNwag0_un0ey3o0TrKE6WISUwtoyLAD1p0r32KxiLjPSj7cMLKo944PJSwVQMWy4P495fY5JglYloOjr8gN6Y2uX7cZp5g-VuVn9AgXWyZlDG1BX2OeQW6ihPPzMsbhUEMzUsIUlfxcTL3orU2LMBozuFeGW1G9NZdO9wdrzM5kZrSidXNISqoIudZbLuUwqwISvDsn5di80Jdqqaokd7O3VbLX3_5T3xe2gOM0CK5VDkSq9orSKLCkmKIgiDDg6nYRrLSCBbE_4AEXyo7tnI-8EJYGzX4fnE9FOgAr6_8hC1k5s-Dx_iarfhBgIhaeuWbgeTDWTaPZfeojQS23KTpmyvXTX7yEtyw1aFwdJKyNWmgmKTIr2kBnzhXPh7hnZ-XM-DMH1cSq4v5pZgawnYQakuBKJb42qW5DIMbCHpRv4kIHx1PzkekI2vl_418CB5ZnBDLcOqazGgDdBu7C5qemit52qkW4PtC18dlC6tyU_ex4QzJ2Yjt43b9iMsHpiQ3WXKp-tUQf2R0_XS38ciBqdT4nrNANjjdioWc-YFUhFEa1io1tvDQ8YeKXwPBI1be5JnlvrhuorHqApPhm_FCb9xVJlFgDfGtkZn0C1Ppjk=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Sj3g9BesnB0mCXETdNGJD7kA|fc_0777a1a86320e9530169d00c6466b8819189c487a360979479","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: slm-expert\ndescription: Query a small language model (SLM) endpoint with expertise in nephrology, cardiology, and hypertension by sending a focused question together with one or more required medical domains, and optionally structured patient context. Use when the agent needs a specialty-aware answer or supporting interpretation in those domains and must explicitly set the `domains` field on every request.\n---\n\n# SLM Expert\n\nUse this skill to query the specialty SLM at `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query` for nephrology, cardiology, or hypertension questions.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the request is in scope.\n   - Use this skill for nephrology, cardiology, or hypertension questions.\n   - Use it when the question needs explicit specialty routing through the `domains` field.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build the question.\n   - Write one clear, focused question.\n   - Use the user's wording directly when it is already specific.\n   - If the user gives case details, compress them into a concise specialty question.\n   - Do not invent missing facts.\n\n3. Choose the domains.\n   - Always set the `domains` field together with the `question`.\n   - Include one or more of these values only: `nephrology`, `cardiology`, `hypertension`.\n   - Choose the narrowest correct set.\n   - Use multiple domains only when the question genuinely spans them.\n   - Example mappings:\n     - Kidney disease, CKD, AKI, proteinuria, renal medication issues -> `nephrology`\n     - Cardiovascular risk, heart disease, lipid therapy, cardiac findings -> `cardiology`\n     - Blood pressure control, hypertensive organ damage, antihypertensive strategy -> `hypertension`\n     - Hypertensive kidney damage -> `nephrology`, `hypertension`\n\n4. Add patient context when available.\n   - Pass structured context only when it materially helps.\n   - Keep it concise and factual.\n   - Use a JSON object for `patient_context`.\n   - Omit it when there is no meaningful context to send.\n\n5. Call the endpoint.\n   - Run the helper script from the skill directory:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert.py \\\n  --question \"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\" \\\n  --domain nephrology \\\n  --domain hypertension\n```\n\n   - Example with patient context:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert.py \\\n  --question \"Why do patients with CKD require careful medication management?\" \\\n  --domain nephrology \\\n  --patient-context '{\"age\":67,\"conditions\":[\"CKD stage 3\",\"hypertension\"],\"medications\":[\"lisinopril\",\"furosemide\"]}'\n```\n\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"string\",\n  \"domains\": [\"string\"],\n  \"patient_context\": {\n    \"additionalProp1\": {}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n   - Endpoint:\n\n```text\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\n```\n\n6. Read the response.\n   - Prefer `answer` as the main model output.\n   - Read `domain` as the model-selected or echoed specialty scope.\n   - Treat `sources` as optional supporting metadata.\n   - If the answer is `Not found in context.`, report that plainly instead of inventing content.\n\n7. Use the result safely.\n   - Treat the SLM output as supportive specialty input, not a confirmed diagnosis.\n   - Cross-check it against the available patient details and the user’s question.\n   - Preserve uncertainty.\n   - If the output is thin or context-limited, say so.\n\n## Request examples\n\nUse patterns like these:\n\n```json\n{\"question\": \"When is medication recommended for cardiovascular risk factor management?\", \"domains\": [\"cardiology\"]}\n{\"question\": \"Why do patients with CKD require careful medication management?\", \"domains\": [\"nephrology\"]}\n{\"question\": \"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\", \"domains\": [\"nephrology\", \"hypertension\"]}\n```\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn a response that includes, when useful:\n\n- **SLM answer**: the key answer text\n- **Domain(s)**: the domains used or returned\n- **Agent interpretation**: a short grounded interpretation\n- **Cautions / gaps**: especially when the model says context is missing or the answer is limited\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: slm-expert\\ndescription: Query a small language model (SLM) endpoint with expertise in nephrology, cardiology, and hypertension by sending a focused question together with one or more required medical domains, and optionally structured patient context. Use when the agent needs a specialty-aware answer or supporting interpretation in those domains and must explicitly set the `domains` field on every request.\\n---\\n\\n# SLM Expert\\n\\nUse this skill to query the specialty SLM at `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query` for nephrology, cardiology, or hypertension questions.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Confirm the request is in scope.\\n   - Use this skill for nephrology, cardiology, or hypertension questions.\\n   - Use it when the question needs explicit specialty routing through the `domains` field.\\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\\n\\n2. Build the question.\\n   - Write one clear, focused question.\\n   - Use the user's wording directly when it is already specific.\\n   - If the user gives case details, compress them into a concise specialty question.\\n   - Do not invent missing facts.\\n\\n3. Choose the domains.\\n   - Always set the `domains` field together with the `question`.\\n   - Include one or more of these values only: `nephrology`, `cardiology`, `hypertension`.\\n   - Choose the narrowest correct set.\\n   - Use multiple domains only when the question genuinely spans them.\\n   - Example mappings:\\n     - Kidney disease, CKD, AKI, proteinuria, renal medication issues -> `nephrology`\\n     - Cardiovascular risk, heart disease, lipid therapy, cardiac findings -> `cardiology`\\n     - Blood pressure control, hypertensive organ damage, antihypertensive strategy -> `hypertension`\\n     - Hypertensive kidney damage -> `nephrology`, `hypertension`\\n\\n4. Add patient context when available.\\n   - Pass structured context only when it materially helps.\\n   - Keep it concise and factual.\\n   - Use a JSON object for `patient_context`.\\n   - Omit it when there is no meaningful context to send.\\n\\n5. Call the endpoint.\\n   - Run the helper script from the skill directory:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert.py \\\\\\n  --question \\\"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\\\" \\\\\\n  --domain nephrology \\\\\\n  --domain hypertension\\n```\\n\\n   - Example with patient context:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert.py \\\\\\n  --question \\\"Why do patients with CKD require careful medication management?\\\" \\\\\\n  --domain nephrology \\\\\\n  --patient-context '{\\\"age\\\":67,\\\"conditions\\\":[\\\"CKD stage 3\\\",\\\"hypertension\\\"],\\\"medications\\\":[\\\"lisinopril\\\",\\\"furosemide\\\"]}'\\n```\\n\\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"domains\\\": [\\\"string\\\"],\\n  \\\"patient_context\\\": {\\n    \\\"additionalProp1\\\": {}\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n   - Endpoint:\\n\\n```text\\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\\n```\\n\\n6. Read the response.\\n   - Prefer `answer` as the main model output.\\n   - Read `domain` as the model-selected or echoed specialty scope.\\n   - Treat `sources` as optional supporting metadata.\\n   - If the answer is `Not found in context.`, report that plainly instead of inventing content.\\n\\n7. Use the result safely.\\n   - Treat the SLM output as supportive specialty input, not a confirmed diagnosis.\\n   - Cross-check it against the available patient details and the user’s question.\\n   - Preserve uncertainty.\\n   - If the output is thin or context-limited, say so.\\n\\n## Request examples\\n\\nUse patterns like these:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"question\\\": \\\"When is medication recommended for cardiovascular risk factor management?\\\", \\\"domains\\\": [\\\"cardiology\\\"]}\\n{\\\"question\\\": \\\"Why do patients with CKD require careful medication management?\\\", \\\"domains\\\": [\\\"nephrology\\\"]}\\n{\\\"question\\\": \\\"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\\\", \\\"domains\\\": [\\\"nephrology\\\", \\\"hypertension\\\"]}\\n```\\n\\n## Output pattern\\n\\nReturn a response that includes, when useful:\\n\\n- **SLM answer**: the key answer text\\n- **Domain(s)**: the domains used or returned\\n- **Agent interpretation**: a short grounded interpretation\\n- **Cautions / gaps**: especially when the model says context is missing or the answer is limited\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1851,"output":1095,"cacheRead":17280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20226,"cost":{"input":0.0046275000000000005,"output":0.016425000000000002,"cacheRead":0.00432,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.025372500000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775242338712}}
{"type":"message","id":"1e336270","parentId":"d894441e","timestamp":"2026-04-03T18:52:39.706Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Sj3g9BesnB0mCXETdNGJD7kA|fc_0777a1a86320e9530169d00c6466b8819189c487a360979479","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 4094 bytes to /home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert/SKILL.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775242359699}}
{"type":"message","id":"b1de628f","parentId":"1e336270","timestamp":"2026-04-03T18:53:01.509Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_UR190HUQ2REEIhzOYyqH9JQa|fc_0777a1a86320e9530169d00c7a7b208191818e333a3304de52","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert/scripts/query_slm_expert.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport urllib.request\nimport urllib.error\n\nENDPOINT = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\"\nALLOWED_DOMAINS = {\"nephrology\", \"cardiology\", \"hypertension\"}\n\n\ndef parse_args():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Query the specialty SLM with a question, required domains, and optional patient context.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--question\", required=True, help=\"Focused question to ask the SLM\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--domain\",\n        action=\"append\",\n        dest=\"domains\",\n        required=True,\n        help=\"Domain to include. Repeat for multiple domains: nephrology, cardiology, hypertension\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--patient-context\",\n        help=\"Optional JSON object string for patient_context\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--patient-context-file\",\n        help=\"Optional path to a JSON file containing patient_context\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--timeout\",\n        type=int,\n        default=60,\n        help=\"HTTP timeout in seconds (default: 60)\",\n    )\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\n\ndef load_patient_context(args):\n    if args.patient_context and args.patient_context_file:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Provide either --patient-context or --patient-context-file, not both.\")\n\n    if args.patient_context_file:\n        try:\n            with open(args.patient_context_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                data = json.load(f)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            raise SystemExit(f\"Failed to read patient context file: {exc}\")\n    elif args.patient_context:\n        try:\n            data = json.loads(args.patient_context)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n            raise SystemExit(f\"Invalid --patient-context JSON: {exc}\")\n    else:\n        return None\n\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise SystemExit(\"patient_context must be a JSON object.\")\n    return data\n\n\ndef normalize_domains(domains):\n    normalized = []\n    seen = set()\n    for domain in domains or []:\n        value = domain.strip().lower()\n        if not value:\n            continue\n        if value not in ALLOWED_DOMAINS:\n            allowed = \", \".join(sorted(ALLOWED_DOMAINS))\n            raise SystemExit(f\"Invalid domain '{domain}'. Allowed values: {allowed}\")\n        if value not in seen:\n            normalized.append(value)\n            seen.add(value)\n    if not normalized:\n        raise SystemExit(\"At least one valid --domain is required.\")\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef main():\n    args = parse_args()\n    patient_context = load_patient_context(args)\n    domains = normalize_domains(args.domains)\n\n    payload = {\n        \"question\": args.question,\n        \"domains\": domains,\n    }\n    if patient_context is not None:\n        payload[\"patient_context\"] = patient_context\n\n    body = json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    request = urllib.request.Request(\n        ENDPOINT,\n        data=body,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=args.timeout) as response:\n            raw = response.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n            content_type = response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\", \"\")\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:\n        error_body = exc.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        print(error_body or str(exc), file=sys.stderr)\n        raise SystemExit(exc.code)\n    except urllib.error.URLError as exc:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Request failed: {exc}\")\n\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        if \"json\" in content_type.lower():\n            raise SystemExit(\"Endpoint returned invalid JSON.\")\n        print(raw)\n        return\n\n    print(json.dumps(parsed, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert/scripts/query_slm_expert.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nimport urllib.request\\nimport urllib.error\\n\\nENDPOINT = \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\\\"\\nALLOWED_DOMAINS = {\\\"nephrology\\\", \\\"cardiology\\\", \\\"hypertension\\\"}\\n\\n\\ndef parse_args():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\\n        description=\\\"Query the specialty SLM with a question, required domains, and optional patient context.\\\"\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--question\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Focused question to ask the SLM\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\n        \\\"--domain\\\",\\n        action=\\\"append\\\",\\n        dest=\\\"domains\\\",\\n        required=True,\\n        help=\\\"Domain to include. Repeat for multiple domains: nephrology, cardiology, hypertension\\\",\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\n        \\\"--patient-context\\\",\\n        help=\\\"Optional JSON object string for patient_context\\\",\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\n        \\\"--patient-context-file\\\",\\n        help=\\\"Optional path to a JSON file containing patient_context\\\",\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\n        \\\"--timeout\\\",\\n        type=int,\\n        default=60,\\n        help=\\\"HTTP timeout in seconds (default: 60)\\\",\\n    )\\n    return parser.parse_args()\\n\\n\\ndef load_patient_context(args):\\n    if args.patient_context and args.patient_context_file:\\n        raise SystemExit(\\\"Provide either --patient-context or --patient-context-file, not both.\\\")\\n\\n    if args.patient_context_file:\\n        try:\\n            with open(args.patient_context_file, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n                data = json.load(f)\\n        except Exception as exc:\\n            raise SystemExit(f\\\"Failed to read patient context file: {exc}\\\")\\n    elif args.patient_context:\\n        try:\\n            data = json.loads(args.patient_context)\\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\\n            raise SystemExit(f\\\"Invalid --patient-context JSON: {exc}\\\")\\n    else:\\n        return None\\n\\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\\n        raise SystemExit(\\\"patient_context must be a JSON object.\\\")\\n    return data\\n\\n\\ndef normalize_domains(domains):\\n    normalized = []\\n    seen = set()\\n    for domain in domains or []:\\n        value = domain.strip().lower()\\n        if not value:\\n            continue\\n        if value not in ALLOWED_DOMAINS:\\n            allowed = \\\", \\\".join(sorted(ALLOWED_DOMAINS))\\n            raise SystemExit(f\\\"Invalid domain '{domain}'. Allowed values: {allowed}\\\")\\n        if value not in seen:\\n            normalized.append(value)\\n            seen.add(value)\\n    if not normalized:\\n        raise SystemExit(\\\"At least one valid --domain is required.\\\")\\n    return normalized\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    args = parse_args()\\n    patient_context = load_patient_context(args)\\n    domains = normalize_domains(args.domains)\\n\\n    payload = {\\n        \\\"question\\\": args.question,\\n        \\\"domains\\\": domains,\\n    }\\n    if patient_context is not None:\\n        payload[\\\"patient_context\\\"] = patient_context\\n\\n    body = json.dumps(payload).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    request = urllib.request.Request(\\n        ENDPOINT,\\n        data=body,\\n        headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"},\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=args.timeout) as response:\\n            raw = response.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n            content_type = response.headers.get(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:\\n        error_body = exc.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        print(error_body or str(exc), file=sys.stderr)\\n        raise SystemExit(exc.code)\\n    except urllib.error.URLError as exc:\\n        raise SystemExit(f\\\"Request failed: {exc}\\\")\\n\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n        if \\\"json\\\" in content_type.lower():\\n            raise SystemExit(\\\"Endpoint returned invalid JSON.\\\")\\n        print(raw)\\n        return\\n\\n    print(json.dumps(parsed, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":164,"output":1041,"cacheRead":20096,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21301,"cost":{"input":0.00041000000000000005,"output":0.015615,"cacheRead":0.005024,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.021049000000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775242359704}}
